NET(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    net - show and configure network interfaces

SYNOPSIS
    net
    net config IF ADDRESS NETMASK [GATEWAY]
    net down IF
    net apply

DESCRIPTION
    Without arguments prints the text snapshot of /dev/net: one line per
    interface with its counters, "link" lines with the MAC addresses,
    the "inet" line with the configured address, netmask and gateway,
    "arp" lines with the neighbour cache, and the IP, ARP, ICMP, UDP, TCP
    and packet pool counters.

    config assigns an address to an Ethernet interface; the gateway must
    lie inside the subnet. down removes the address, netmask and gateway
    while the interface stays attached, so DHCP can start again. apply
    reads /etc/network, which init runs as a boot task:

        iface eth0 dhcp                   left to the dhcp service
        iface eth0 static ADDR MASK [GW]  configure once
        nameserver ADDR                   written to /etc/resolv.conf

    The dhcp entry is served by dhcpc(1) -a, the dhcp service of
    init.conf(5), started right after apply. A missing file or a missing
    interface means no network; the shell is never delayed. MiniOS is
    single user: every process may reconfigure.

FILES
    /dev/net, /etc/network, /etc/resolv.conf

SEE ALSO
    dhcpc(1), init.conf(5), ping(1), nc(1), http(1), index(7)
